{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 3.8% a year from $22.7 billion in FY2016 to $31.7 billion in FY2025 [F1][F9][F198], while operating income grew faster at 5.8% [F199]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The window is a slow, regulated grind upward rather than a step change, with operating margin rising from 22.9% to 27.2% [F20][F28]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2022 was the sharpest revenue inflection, up 17.1% [D239], driven by rate cases, favorable weather and volumes [P26][P34]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2020 was the low point, with net income down 63.3% [D157] on coal-ash settlement impairments and pandemic volume losses [P60]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Electric Utilities and Infrastructure supplied 90.9% of FY2025 revenue [D541] and contributed 3.6pp of the 5.6% growth [D543][D358]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Residential electric was the largest single driver, at 43.3% of revenue [D774] and 2.8pp of FY2025 growth [D776]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Gas Utilities and Infrastructure added 2.0pp in FY2025 [D566], with Piedmont Natural Gas up 32.1% [D682]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 8.8% against 5.6% revenue growth in FY2025 [D359][D358], an incremental margin of 41.4% [D378]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS grew 8.2% a year against 9.7% net income growth [F202][F200], as the diluted share count rose from 691 million to 777 million [X106][X115]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FY2025 operating margin of 27.2% [F28] is the window high [D932], 4.3pp above the 22.9% median [D933]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 margin rose 0.8pp [D370] as revenue growth outpaced operating-cost growth by 0.3pp [D379]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "D&A rose to 24.3% of revenue in FY2025 from 21.4% in FY2024 [D341][D303], reflecting a growing asset base [P12]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin of 15.7% [F47] sits 11.5pp below operating margin [D967], as interest expense reached $3.6 billion [X63]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Interest expense rose on higher outstanding debt balances and interest rates [P10], and the effective tax rate was 11.2% [D345]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $12.3 billion was 2.48x net income in FY2025 [F77][D346], near the 2.59x window median [D958]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Free cash flow was negative $1.69 billion [F97], a -5.3% margin [D343], against a -5.8% window median [D939]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Capex of $14.0 billion was 44.2% of revenue [F87][D342] and 1.82x D&A [D348]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2022 conversion fell to 20.7% of revenue [D224] as rising fuel costs created undercollections that increased borrowings [P36]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net debt reached $89.6 billion in FY2025 [D352], 282.3% of revenue [D353], with cash of just $245 million [F137]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "That net-debt ratio is worse than the utilities peer median of -235.4% of revenue [D969], at the 33rd percentile of three peers [D968]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Total debt grew 6.6% in FY2025 [D376], with $11.9 billion issued against $5.7 billion repaid [X133][X143]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity of 9.7% [D357] trails the 12.6% peer median [D956], at the 0th percentile of four peers [D955]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The current ratio fell to 0.55x in FY2025 [F177], the window low [D943], as current liabilities rose 8.7% [D369]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Cash covers only 0.1 years of the latest free-cash-flow burn [D356], leaving little standalone liquidity buffer."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net debt has risen nine consecutive years to $89.6 billion [D14][D352], funding a capex programme that keeps free cash flow negative."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Free cash flow ran below 80% of net income in FY2023, FY2024 and FY2025 [D269][D309][D347], so earnings are not converting to distributable cash."},
